Description: network and system administration labs on Docker machines
 SysResEval (sre) runs teaching labs made of Docker machines wired by the
 Kathara framework: a lab file describes the machines, the networks, the
 initial configuration and the automatic evaluation of what the students did.
 The students work in the sysreseval graphical interface (terminals on the
 machines, course text, questions, evaluations); the instructors write the
 labs, run exams and collect the evaluation archives with the sre command.
 .
 The labs of the project are in /usr/share/sysreseval/lab, the site's own
 labs go in /var/lib/sre/lab; the site parameters are in /etc/sysreseval.

Package: sysreseval-web
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         adduser,
         python3-aiohttp,
         python3-aiohttp-jinja2,
         python3-jinja2
Recommends: python3-ldap3
Suggests: nginx | apache2 | caddy, sysreseval-agent
Description: web site of SysResEval
 The web site through which the students work on the labs from a browser: the
 projects run on a pool of hosts (sysreseval-agent), every tab of the graphical
 interface is rendered in the browser and the terminals go through WebSockets.
 The users log in with an LDAP directory (the portal itself, or an Apache
 reverse proxy in front of it), or everybody is anonymous.
 .
 This host needs neither Docker nor the labs.  Configuration: /etc/sysreseval/web.toml
 (see /usr/share/doc/sysreseval-web/examples/).

Package: sysreseval-agent
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         sysreseval (>= ${source:Version}),
         sysreseval-web (= ${binary:Version}),
         adduser
Recommends: openbox,
            tigervnc-standalone-server
Description: pool-host agent of the SysResEval web site
 The daemon of a host of the pool behind sysreseval-web: it runs sre on behalf
 of the web users, exactly as the graphical interface does for the students of
 a workstation, owns their terminals and schedules their evaluations.  With
 tigervnc-standalone-server and openbox it also runs the virtual X desktops of
 the projects (the Display tab of the web site: the graphical applications of
 the labs), as the unprivileged user sreweb-x11.
 Configuration: /etc/sysreseval/agent.toml (see /usr/share/doc/sysreseval-agent/examples/).

Package: sysreseval-doc
Architecture: all
Section: doc
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: documentation of SysResEval
 The HTML and PDF documentation of SysResEval: installation and setup, the
 graphical interface, the sre command, lab authoring, the exam mode, the
 archive format and the API of the lab libraries.
